# behavior: under one job, test files that share a plain session-scoped `conftest.incn` fixture run in one process, so the fixture is set up once for the run, across directories and when one file's test fails, as 0.5.1's single worker does (#3149).
# cli-commands:
#   test tests --nocapture
# expect-stdout:
#
#   running 1 test
#   session setup
#   delta one
#   test_delta.incn::test_delta_one PASSED
#   alpha one
#   test_alpha.incn::test_alpha_one PASSED
#   alpha two
#   test_alpha.incn::test_alpha_two PASSED
#   beta one
#   test_beta.incn::test_beta_one PASSED
#   test_gamma.incn::test_gamma_fails FAILED
#   gamma passes
#   test incan_case_batch ... ok
#
#   test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in <duration>
#
#   test_gamma.incn::test_gamma_passes PASSED
# expect-stderr-contains:
#   gamma fails
# expect-exit: 1

def main() -> None:
    println("main")
